    "created_at": "2016-09-18T20:13:26Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-09-18T20:13:26Z",
    "body": "> what is the value of a radio button group?\n\nThere is no such thing as the value of a radio button group. A particular control has a value. In this case the value of the first is \"1\" and the value of the second is \"2\".\n\n>  Is it the value that would be sent on form submission? \n\nNo. The algorithm for assembling the form data set takes as input various control values, but the output is not really connected to the value used for determining whether something suffers from being missing. You can see the algorithm at https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/forms.html#constructing-the-form-data-set\n\n> Shouldn't both cases be treated the same way, i.e. checked but disabled radio/checkboxes should be ignored when considering if a group passes constraint validations? \n\nI could see arguments for both sides. However, there's the overwhelming argument in favor of the current semantics, which is that they have been this way since the beginning, and countless web pages depend on them, which we don't want to break. (For example, web pages that use client-side form validation but don't use server-side form submission.)\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
