    "updated_at": "2016-09-19T15:19:15Z",
    "body": "I might not be reading it properly, but the definition above doesn't mention checkedness of other radio buttons in the group, so I don't see how it could be appropriate. It only refers to the other buttons' `required` attribute, which is fine.\n\nI'm not sure what the \"value\" of a radio button that is unchecked is. You stated that in my example the second radio's button is \"2\", is that the case even when unchecked? If so, how could it be ever \"Suffering from being missing\"? Or if it has value \"2\" only when checked, then all unchecked radios would always be \"Suffering from being missing\", even if one radio in the group is checked. I imagine that this is not the intent, but if I read strictly what's written, that's what I deduce. Or am I missing something obvious?\n",
