    "created_at": "2016-09-19T15:37:47Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-09-19T15:37:47Z",
    "body": "> I'm not sure what the \"value\" of a radio button that is unchecked is. You stated that in my example the second radio's button is \"2\", is that the case even when unchecked?\n\nCorrect\n\n>  If so, how could it be ever \"Suffering from being missing\"?\n\nAh! I found the issue. The description you quoted is not normative. Right above it, it says \"(The definitions below are non-normative; other parts of this specification define more precisely when each state applies or does not.)\" The more precise, normative version is at https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/forms.html#radio-button-state-(type=radio):suffering-from-being-missing:\n\n> If an element in the radio button group is required, and all of the input elements in the radio button group have a checkedness that is false, then the element is suffering from being missing.\n\nThat said, I think we should reopen this to clarify the non-normative version. Maybe something vague like this:\n\n> When a control has no value but has a required attribute; or more complicated rules for radio button groups and select elements.\n",
