    "created_at": "2016-09-19T16:22:44Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-09-19T16:22:44Z",
    "body": "Right, I see.\n\nIndeed the normative section is clearer. I'm wondering if it is 100% accurate though.\n\nTake the following example:\n\n```\n<form>\n<input type=\"radio\" name=\"a\" value=\"1\" required disabled>\n<input type=\"radio\" name=\"a\" value=\"2\">\n</form>\n```\n\n> Constraint validation: If an element is disabled, it is barred from constraint validation.\n\nSo the first radio is not validated. Fine.\n\nUnless I'm missing something, the second radio isn't technically required, so the \"If an element in the radio button group is required\" does not apply to it, so it shouldn't be suffering from being missing... That's not the intention though.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
