    "created_at": "2016-09-19T16:37:09Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-09-19T16:37:09Z",
    "body": "> The first element in the radio button group is required though, so \"an\" element in the radio button group is indeed required.\n\nSure, but the first element isn't the one that needs to fail validation.\n\nStated otherwise: FF/Chrome have `checkValidity()` return `false` for the second radio, which doesn't actually correspond to the written rule. I'd say they are correct and the standard isn't.\n\nIt's a real corner case, maybe not worth delving into\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
